Description: Sound and controller hotplug for an appliance
 Mixxx 2.5 opens sound devices and controllers only at start-up. DecksmithOS
 uses the controller's USB audio as its sound card, so plugging the controller
 in after start-up (or unplugging and plugging it in again) left Mixxx silent
 and the controller dead until a restart.
 With DECKSMITHOS_SOUND_HOTPLUG_HOOK set in the environment:
  - /proc/asound/cards is checked every second; on a change the hook runs
    (it writes soundconfig.xml for the controller's audio and prints
    DECKSMITHOS_* variables, set in Mixxx's environment), the sound devices
    are queried again and set up from soundconfig.xml, and the controllers are
    enumerated again (PortMidi is restarted so that new MIDI devices appear).
    Not while the preferences dialog is open; retried after it is closed.
  - Start-up without the output device does not overwrite soundconfig.xml
    with an empty configuration (with DECKSMITHOS_NO_SOUND_DIALOGS).
Author: DecksmithOS
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-20
